    Binaries, tidal disturbance and unresolved rotation all inflate a measured sigma, and they inflate it
    most where sigma is smallest.  If that is the common cause, subtracting one floor s_0 in quadrature from
    every measured dispersion should collapse the ledger.  One parameter, fitted the same way as D, L and S.

