  [PASS] 7a THE OBSERVATIONAL EXPLANATION FAILS IN THE SAME WAY AND FOR THE OPPOSITE REASON, WHICH IS THE USEFUL PART.  A dispersion-inflation floor lowers EVERY offset, so it helps the positive rows and hurts the negative ones: it cannot be the common cause either, and the star clusters -- which have the smallest dispersions in the table and would be inflated most -- are exactly the rows it makes worse   (best s_0 = 0.00 km/s leaves rms = 0.727 dex; the star-cluster mean goes -0.428 -> -0.428 dex)

